/-!
# Objects of `D_QCoh` with countable cohomology are homotopy colimits of perfect objects

Let `X` be a quasi-compact and quasi-separated algebraic space whose structure sheaf has countable
sets of sections over the affine schemes étale over `X`. An object `K` of `D_QCoh(𝒪_X)` is a
homotopy colimit of perfect objects of `D(𝒪_X)` if and only if its cohomology sheaves have
countable sets of sections over the affine schemes étale over `X`. This is Stacks 0CRV.

For an affine chart `V = Spec(A)` of `X`, the sections over `V` of the cohomology sheaves of an
object `L` of `D_QCoh` are the cohomology of `RΓ(V, L)` in `D(A)`; a perfect object restricts to a
perfect complex of `A`-modules, with countable cohomology as `A` is countable, and `RΓ(V, -)`
together with cohomology commutes with homotopy colimits. This gives (1) ⇒ (2). For the
converse, `D_QCoh(𝒪_X)` is generated by a compact object `P`, which is perfect, and by Stacks 0CRU
every `Hom(P[m], -)` is countable on the compact objects and on `K`; the cell tower of the proof of
Stacks 0CRM, which needs nothing more, writes `K` as a homotopy colimit of compact, hence perfect,
objects.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.countable_homology_sections_of_isPerfect`: the cohomology sheaves of a
  perfect object have countable sections over affine étale charts.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_isHomotopyColimit_isPerfect_iff_countable`: **Stacks 0CRV**.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CRV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CRV)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

